BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-188597@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260604T140000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260604T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260604T160000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Art of Boston in Provincetown
LOCATION:Offsite: Mary Heaton Vorse House
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: $46.73 per person\nAvailability: 50 
 spots left\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com
 /events/188597\n\n11:00AM - 12:00PM Optional Provincetown Art Association 
 & Museum Tour\n2:00PM Private Reception & MHVH Gallery Viewing\, 3:00PM -
  4:00PM Panel Discussion\nThe unofficial start to summer welcomes Part Two
  of The ‘Quin’s Summer Art Exchange offsite in America's oldest contin
 uous art colony - Provincetown\, at the storied Mary Heaton Vorse House be
 ginning this Saturday\, May 23rd.\n\nTogether with the Provincetown Art So
 ciety\, 'Quin members are invited to join us on June 4th for a private rec
 eption and self-guided gallery viewing of the new offsite exhibition featu
 ring local artists of The 'Quin's permanent art collection: Zainab Sumu\,
  Yu-Wen Wu\, Brian Zink\, Adrienne Shishko and Lavaughan Jenkins.\n\nMem
 bers will gather in the Mary Heaton Vorse House courtyard for a panel disc
 ussion exploring P-town's rich artistic history\, and the vital role of ar
 t organizations together with the collection curators\, Kate Chertavian\, 
 Gene Tartaglia\, and 'Quin Creative Director (also behind the restoration 
 of the MHVH) Ken Fulk.\n\nConsidering making a day of it? We welcome those
  attending the afternoon program to attend a complimentary tour of the Pro
 vincetown Art Association & Museum together with CEO\, Christine McCarthy 
 from 11:00AM-Noon. Between events\, members will have time to grab a bite 
 and explore the various galleries that make up the community in advance of
  afternoon 'Quin Programming at the MHVH. If you plan to attend this aspec
 t of the day\, please do ensure this is noted when you purchase a ticket.\
 n\n*This event is $50/per person and reserved for members\, plus one regis
 tered guest. Transportation is the responsibility of members. Please look 
 forward to light bites and beverage during the afternoon reception.\n\nNot
  able to make it? The Mary Heaton Vorse House reciprocal exhibition will b
 e on display in Provincetown from May 23rd - July 12th.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/188597
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
