BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-186709@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260609T193000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260609T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260609T203000
SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: The Gap Years with Tom French
LOCATION:The Terrace Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/186709\n\nBookmark the date fo
 r an inspiring conversation exploring The Gap Years with author Tom French
  & moderated by Wendy Dodson\, owner of Hummingbird Books - a powerful ref
 lection on adventure\, endurance\, and the pursuit of meaning beyond the e
 xpected path.\n\nAt the close of a four-decade career\, French set out to 
 rediscover the passions that once defined him. What began as a single “g
 ap year” evolved into a transformative three-year journey—one that too
 k him from cross-country ski races to the slopes of the world’s highest 
 peaks\, including two extraordinary expeditions to Mount Everest. Along th
 e way\, he faced physical limits\, unpredictable elements\, and moments of
  profound uncertainty\, from navigating a cyclone high on the mountain to 
 summiting under a moonlit sky via an uncharted approach.\n\nYet The Gap Ye
 ars is about more than endurance at altitude. It is a meditation on renewa
 l - on the beauty of wild places\, the discipline of sport\, and the deepe
 r question of how we choose to spend our time. French’s story invites us
  to reconsider what it means to begin again\, and to reconnect with the pu
 rsuits that once made us feel most alive.\n\n*This event is complimentary 
 and reserved for members only. Light refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/186709
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-187622@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260610T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260610T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260610T183000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Checkmate" with Ben Mezrich
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 5 spots left\nSt
 atus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/event
 s/187622\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion \nStep into the high-sta
 kes world of Checkmate with bestselling author Ben Mezrich—an electrifyi
 ng true story that unravels the biggest scandal in modern chess.\n\nIn Sep
 tember 2022\, the chess world was shaken when nineteen-year-old American p
 rodigy Hans Niemann defeated reigning world champion Magnus Carlsen in a s
 tunning upset. Days later\, Carlsen accused Niemann of cheating—an alleg
 ation that ignited a global firestorm\, drawing in Chess.com\, the media\,
  and a rapidly expanding digital audience. What followed was a dramatic co
 llision of reputation\, rivalry\, and power.\n\nBut Checkmate is about far
  more than controversy. It’s a portrait of ambition at its sharpest edge
 —a young player willing to risk everything to rise\, and a legendary fig
 ure determined to defend his legacy. Set against the backdrop of a centuri
 es-old game transformed by streaming\, sponsorships\, and Silicon Valley i
 nfluence\, Mezrich brings readers inside a world that is as cutthroat as i
 t is cerebral.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members on
 ly. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/187622
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
