BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-186725@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260611T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260611T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260611T193000
SUMMARY:Wit & Word: A Performance in Written Humor
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/186725\n\n5:30PM Reception\, 6
 :00PM Performance\nWit & Word offers an evening where humor is written\, s
 poken\, and felt—bringing together a standout group of writers for a liv
 e\, spoken-word style performance that celebrates the craft of comedy on t
 he page. Moving beyond stand-up\, the night unfolds through essays\, satir
 e\, and personal storytelling—sharp\, candid\, and unexpectedly moving.\
 n\nGuiding the evening is award-winning comedian and The Moth regular Be
 thany Van Delft\, whose distinctive voice and grounded storytelling bring 
 warmth\, wit\, and a natural sense of connection to the stage.\n\nThe line
 up features Tracy McArdle Brady\, Founder and Chief Humorist of Wit & Word
 \; Steve Almond\, New York Times bestselling author\; Lisa Borders\, awa
 rd-winning novelist and McSweeney’s contributor\; Neil Martinez-Belkin\,
  New York Times bestselling co-author and former music editor of XXL Ma
 gazine\; and Viktoria Shulevich\, humor writer published in The New Yorke
 r and McSweeney’s. Together\, they explore the absurdities and revelati
 ons of modern adulting through humor that is as insightful as it is entert
 aining.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Lig
 ht refreshments will be served and beverages will be available for purchas
 e.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/186725
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
